{"h":3396,"lines":[{"x":0.43204923439115833,"h":0.01782497725020582,"w":0.13384391784667976,"y":0.081203790430308564,"c":1,"t":"READING"},{"w":0.30658437093098956,"y":0.14389534870165022,"t":"READING PASSAGE 1","x":0.080246909081830325,"h":0.01453488398216074,"c":1},{"w":0.81714426676432295,"x":0.080101696904551059,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading","c":1,"h":0.022724081967267384,"y":0.1778169433446839},{"x":0.079931231898531796,"y":0.19686680049784844,"c":1,"t":"Passage 1 below.","h":0.019197879607040003,"w":0.1692803446451823},{"c":1,"w":0.44444442749023433,"x":0.2757201729765571,"t":"Roman shipbuilding and navigation","y":0.23837209283528171,"h":0.020461829447212754},{"w":0.79423868815104171,"y":0.27616279055175208,"x":0.078189297792283216,"t":"Shipbuilding today is based on science and ships are built using computers and sophisticated","c":1,"h":0.01598837238037687},{"h":0.021856157462363801,"y":0.29201981600840821,"x":0.078102431982889589,"w":0.83353836059570319,"c":1,"t":"tools. Shipbuilding in ancient Rome, however, was more of an art relying on estimation, inherited"},{"t":"techniques and personal experience. The Romans were not traditionally sailors but mostly land-","h":0.016195524146054185,"w":0.82098765055338541,"c":1,"y":0.31242638383538479,"x":0.076131689026142715},{"h":0.017667844522968212,"x":0.078189300307094908,"y":0.32979976451798465,"c":1,"w":0.83333333333333337,"t":"based people, who learned to build ships from the people that they conquered, namely the Greeks"},{"c":1,"w":0.16666666666666669,"x":0.076131687144936247,"h":0.01598837238037687,"t":"and the Egyptians.","y":0.34738372076705781},{"w":0.83539093017578137,"c":1,"h":0.017494932361148963,"t":"There are a few surviving written documents that give descriptions and representations of ancient","x":0.078189308477194852,"y":0.38221437011847081},{"w":0.81069956461588544,"t":"Roman ships, including the sails and rigging. Excavated vessels also provide some clues about","x":0.07818930524349782,"h":0.017667844522968212,"y":0.39958775003725622,"c":1},{"y":0.41860465101698785,"t":"ancient shipbuilding techniques. Studies of these have taught us that ancient Roman shipbuilders","x":0.078189309413954217,"h":0.016024324441826665,"w":0.82921808878580727,"c":1},{"y":0.43424812567839677,"h":0.019700148080347368,"x":0.078137224691755491,"t":"built the outer hull first, then proceeded with the frame and the rest of the ship. Planks used to","w":0.80462488810221355,"c":1},{"t":"build the outer hull were initially sewn together. Starting from the 6th century BCE, they were","y":0.4515870720232722,"h":0.021193662717569839,"c":1,"w":0.8047663879394531,"x":0.078057741550540058},{"w":0.81091313680013022,"c":1,"h":0.020920595094930161,"t":"fixed using a method called mortise and tenon, whereby one plank locked into another without","x":0.078070679472447752,"y":0.46917174755214697},{"x":0.07613170324717089,"t":"the need for stitching. Then in the first centuries of the current era, Mediterranean shipbuilders","y":0.48837209321013986,"w":0.81275716145833332,"h":0.017517188131739081,"c":1},{"h":0.017467540902720735,"t":"shifted to another shipbuilding method, still in use today, which consisted of building the frame","x":0.076131698125682309,"c":1,"y":0.50726744170135696,"w":0.81687240600585931},{"w":0.80452672322591134,"c":1,"y":0.5247093021750131,"h":0.01598837238037687,"t":"first and then proceeding with the hull and the other components of the ship. This method was","x":0.078189312939158623},{"w":0.81481480916341131,"y":0.5421083628019322,"t":"more systematic and dramatically shortened ship construction times. The ancient Romans built","c":1,"h":0.016031171463965266,"x":0.078189296138459},{"c":1,"t":"large merchant ships and warships whose size and technology were unequalled until the 16th","y":0.56095406348457166,"w":0.79629628499348959,"x":0.076131692788871413,"h":0.016195524146054185},{"y":0.57838310576318708,"t":"century CE.","c":1,"h":0.017175569972385452,"x":0.077732681818876118,"w":0.10768102010091145},{"h":0.015991796172268979,"t":"Warships were built to be lightweight and very speedy. They had to be able to sail near the coast,","y":0.61336866908503984,"w":0.82716049194335939,"c":1,"x":0.078189301217157281},{"w":0.82921808878580738,"y":0.63074204920649801,"t":"which is why they had no ballast or excess load and were built with a long, narrow hull. They did","x":0.078189309416582475,"h":0.01751376490149259,"c":1},{"x":0.076131688081818152,"y":0.64958775026622606,"h":0.016195524146054185,"c":1,"w":0.82716049194335939,"t":"not sink when damaged and often would lie crippled on the sea's surface following naval battles."},{"x":0.078189311297481842,"h":0.016005492463128657,"c":1,"w":0.81687240600585942,"t":"They had a bronze battering ram, which was used to pierce the timber hulls or break the oars of","y":0.66715116264500718},{"w":0.81893005371093752,"h":0.01598837238037687,"c":1,"t":"enemy vessels. Warships used both wind (sails) and human power (oarsmen) and were therefore","x":0.078189294041353982,"y":0.68459302310973658},{"w":0.81481480916341154,"c":1,"y":0.70200235585311999,"h":0.017474388486504955,"t":"very fast. Eventually, Rome's navy became the largest and most powerful in the Mediterranean,","x":0.07818930310526867},{"c":1,"x":0.076131690900362994,"t":"and the Romans had control over what they therefore called Mare Nostrum meaning 'our sea'.","y":0.71937573598786075,"w":0.80864196777343755,"h":0.017667844522968212},{"y":0.75436046537583745,"w":0.81275721232096354,"x":0.078189295125526428,"h":0.01744185965530165,"t":"There were many kinds of warship. The 'trireme' was the dominant warship from the 7th to 4th","c":1},{"h":0.020153526422974632,"c":1,"t":"century BCE. It had rowers in the top, middle and lower levels, and approximately 50 rowers in","y":0.77175671557364944,"x":0.076085253348005796,"w":0.81695821126302093},{"t":"each bank. The rowers at the bottom had the most uncomfortable position as they were under the","h":0.017503492402524912,"x":0.076131688046033708,"c":1,"y":0.79063604263477449,"w":0.82716049194335928},{"c":1,"x":0.076131693389917626,"t":"other rowers and were exposed to the water entering through the oar-holes. It is worth noting that","w":0.83333333333333326,"y":0.80800942258524999,"h":0.016195524146054185},{"y":0.82558139518885687,"h":0.017469252798666735,"w":0.82716049194335939,"t":"contrary to popular perception, rowers were not slaves but mostly Roman citizens enrolled in the","c":1,"x":0.078189301285346083},{"w":0.65226338704427089,"x":0.078189293992361353,"c":1,"h":0.017441860778592888,"t":"military. The trireme was superseded by larger ships with even more rowers.","y":0.84447674402534423},{"x":0.88888888900140162,"y":0.90843023238112497,"w":0.024691357612609877,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"t":"61"},{"w":0.2523199462890624,"y":0.95563152624206638,"c":1,"x":0.71947457881876942,"t":"IELTSXpress.com","h":0.02837258373750251}],"w":2400}